# MiniML AST Parser

This is a parser and Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) builder for MiniML, written completely in Python. Built to see how compiler frontends work under the hood.

It basically takes raw MiniML code, breaks it down into tokens, and maps it into custom AST node classes so the expressions can be evaluated.

### Files
* `lexer.py` - handles breaking the raw text into tokens
* `parser.py` - contains the logic to build the actual tree
* `ast.py` - defines the custom node classes

### How to use
Just run the main file and pass in your MiniML text:

```bash
python parser.py input.txt